      "content": "11.2 Important 'Firsts' of Gujarat"
    },
    {
      "id": "ng9vrw9",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "First state to establish a solar power policy: Gujarat (2009)",
        "First state to establish a separate Electronics Policy: Gujarat",
        "India's first marine national park: Marine National Park, Gulf of Kutch (1982)",
        "India's first IFSC: GIFT City, Gandhinagar",
        "India's first Bullet Train project: Mumbai–Ahmedabad",
        "World's largest cricket stadium: Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad",
        "India's first city to get UNESCO World Heritage status: Ahmedabad (2017)",
        "First Indian to play Test cricket for England: Ranjitsinhji of Nawanagar, Gujarat",
        "India's first nuclear plant to use light water for cooling: Kakrapar Atomic Power Station",
        "World's largest refinery complex: Reliance Industries, Jamnagar",
        "World's largest salt desert: Rann of Kutch (seasonal)",
        "India's largest port by cargo: Kandla (Deendayal) Port Trust",
        "Only habitat of Asiatic Lion: Gir, Gujarat"
      ]
    },
