      "content": "11.3 Important Rivers, Dams and Canals"
    },
    {
      "id": "aihbimg",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Narmada Main Canal: Longest irrigation canal in India emerging from Sardar Sarovar Dam. The canal is approximately 458 km long (main canal).<img></img>",
        "Sujalam Sufalam Canal: Part of Gujarat's water grid connecting Narmada waters to North Gujarat.",
        "Ukai Reservoir: Largest reservoir in Gujarat on Tapi River."
      ]
    },
